<title>USA: American Intl. sells units for $20.4 million.</title>
<headline>American Intl. sells units for $20.4 million.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>American International Petroleum Corp. said Thursday it agreed in principle to sell its Columbian and Peruvian subsidiaries to Nassau, Bahamas-based Mercantile International Petroleum Inc. for $20.4 million.</p>
<p>The company said the sale is expected to be completed before Feb. 10.</p>
<p>American International said it would use proceeds from the sale to repay debt and finish the expansion of its Lake Charles, La., refinery.</p>
